    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114185,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 580,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114186,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Palatine tonsil</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114187,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients with hamartomatous polyp may have dysphagia, sore throat, globus, or obstructive symptoms. Lesions may be present for weeks to years. The entity appears as a unilateral polypoid mass and may be clinically worrisome for a neoplasm {11048808; 29163996; 31304780}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114188,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "<p>Hamartomas are rare, accounting &le;&nbsp;2% of all tonsillar tumours. Lymphangiectatic fibrous polyps account for the overwhelming majority of hamartomas. Even lesions with a predominance of lymphoid tissue (lymphoid polyp) and those with prominent adipose tissue (fibrolipomatous polyp) are thought to potentially belong to the overall spectrum of lymphangiectatic fibrous polyps. The age range of patients affected is broad (3&ndash;63&nbsp;years, median: 25.5&nbsp;years), and there is no sex predilection {11048808; 29392063; 21562903}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-28T16:20:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114189,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114190,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114191,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Hamartomatous polyp is a polypoid, often pedunculated, mucosal surface mass. The size is variable, ranging from very small to as large as 80&nbsp;mm {11048808; 21562903}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T16:28:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 114192,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 105,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "<p>The lymphangiectatic fibrous polyp has numerous small to medium-sized dilated vascular channels containing proteinaceous fluid with lymphocytes. The overlying mucosa is generally intact, displaying respiratory or squamous epithelium without dysplasia. Small collections of intraepithelial lymphocytes can be seen. The stroma is variable and may consist of fibrous and lymphoid tissue. Adipose tissue and muscle may also be seen, in lesions termed &ldquo;fibrolipomatous polyp&rdquo; {11048808}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-11-28T16:20:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
